    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1928 oil discovery turned Monument from an agricultural ranching hub into a key player in the Permian Basin’s petroleum industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/monument_new_mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A plaque at the statue site honors Monument’s 1885 founding, the 1928 oil boom, the statue, and its rodeo legacy featuring four world champions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/monument_new_mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before oil, Monument’s economy revolved around cattle ranching, with large operations like the Hat Ranch spanning from the Pecos River to the Texas border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/monument_new_mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1985, Monument’s Centennial Committee celebrated 100 years of history, spotlighting its founding, oil boom, and rodeo heritage.",
